#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063973 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064237 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "53bf0d67-be51-5194-884b-e275d58a2ba1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection of Two Inequalities"}] :question/id #uuid "f55392b5-8cb5-516c-8151-051768d813dd" :question/math-academy-id "e-13948" :question/problem "Find the values of $x$ that satisfy $2x - 5 \\leq 1$ and $7x +11 < -3.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve compound \"and\" inequalities, we solve each inequality separately and then find their intersection. \n\n- We start by solving $2x - 5 \\leq 1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-5 & \\le 1 \\\\ 2x-5+5 & \\le 1+5 \\\\ 2x & \\le 6 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{2} & \\le \\frac{6}{2} \\\\ x & \\le 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/60/600e2c9a8560e61697b480de35a3d077d13624ba616514a060c4bcf4fa3f47e4.png)\n\n- Then, we solve $7x +11 < -3$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7x+11 & <-3 \\\\ 7x+11-11 & <-3-11 \\\\ 7x & <-14 \\\\ \\frac{7x}{7} & <\\frac{-14}{7} \\\\ x & <-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/b6/b6014786331de7693c3a1e0d502ea79fb049252fe9f3ecfcd49a873d996896fe.png)\n\nTo find the values of $x$ that satisfy both inequalities, we find where the two solutions overlap:\n\n![](images/2e/2e5425630ece3ab7006378a7930aae0452c3d5261e7bfb579c97daf572b71d22.png)\n\nThus, the final solution is $x < -2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063975 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064238 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "79f6f04e-ecce-5318-b72b-46478661ced0" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Systems of Inequalities"}] :question/id #uuid "f088ca30-8538-57e7-9882-99d5c155c505" :question/math-academy-id "e-13952" :question/problem "What is the solution to the following system of inequalities?\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}5x-35\\ge 0 \\\\ 7x>21\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve the system, we need to find the values of $x$ that satisfy both $5x-35 \\geq 0$ and $7x > 21$ simultaneously.\n\n- First, we solve $5x-35 \\geq 0\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x-35 & \\ge 0 \\\\ 5x-35+35 & \\ge 0+35 \\\\ 5x & \\ge 35 \\\\ \\frac{5x}{5} & \\ge \\frac{35}{5} \\\\ x & \\ge 7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/48/4875553156dc3e4ec15ecdb6c848fd43d519941123d0d9763d209e9f1d6a52f6.png)\n\n- Then, we solve $7x > 21\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7x & >21 \\\\ \\frac{7x}{7} & >\\frac{21}{7} \\\\ x & >3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/f7/f7a68da2d31f0bfe038252ac0dc9151d81bf854a7d33da591cbaef05f52bda28.png)\n\nTo find the values of $x$ that satisfy both inequalities, we find where the two solutions overlap:\n\n![](images/27/27fbd7222a4a02d4a14c17c4043b55a2828e66c2d4dcb019598ea5efef2089e6.png)\n\nThus, the final solution is $x \\geq 7.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063978 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064239 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c9460289-3e48-558e-b149-3e12a25e50a6" :knowledge-point/title "Flipping the Sign of an Inequality in a System"}] :question/id #uuid "0a39d86b-ab9b-5479-9d7b-726247558397" :question/math-academy-id "e-13959" :question/problem "What is the solution to the following system of inequalities?\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2-7x\\ge 2 \\\\ 10x-3\\ge 7\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve the system, we need to find the values of $x$ that satisfy both $2-7x \\geq 2$ and $10x-3 \\geq 7$ simultaneously. \n\n- First, we solve $2-7x \\geq 2\\mathbin{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2-7x & \\ge 2 \\\\ 2-7x-2 & \\ge 2-2 \\\\ -7x & \\ge 0 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot (-7x) & \\le (-1)\\cdot 0 \\\\ 7x & \\le 0 \\\\ \\frac{7x}{7} & \\le \\frac{0}{7} \\\\ x & \\le 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/96/96957d6e6c105fd3734dbe478850287c1c8771873b94fedc4ee0ed5cebf41c40.png)\n\n- Then, we solve $10x-3 \\geq 7\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10x-3 & \\ge 7 \\\\ 10x-3+3 & \\ge 7+3 \\\\ 10x & \\ge 10 \\\\ \\frac{10x}{10} & \\ge \\frac{10}{10} \\\\ x & \\ge 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/9d/9d2d2e7b05bd4bcaf964353266e35bb12f406372ade7255accf6dc3503046f5c.png)\n\nTo find the values of $x$ that satisfy both inequalities, we find where the two solutions overlap:\n\n![](images/98/98654d9ff727e680d0e1ba1ff88b9202248aba6a75a5002a01cd9d628cb6c5b3.png)\n\nIt turns out that the solutions do not overlap at all. Therefore, no values of $x$ satisfy both inequalities simultaneously. So, there is no solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063979 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064240 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3286dfe-5140-5ba7-8e34-c98e63dc15c0" :knowledge-point/title "Systems Containing Compound Inequalities"}] :question/id #uuid "d2726a15-72d6-5c0c-8302-68ba55f8734d" :question/math-academy-id "e-13961" :question/problem "Find the set of values of $x$ that satisfy $1 \\lt 3x-2 \\leq 7$ and $2-3x \\leq -4.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve compound \"and\" inequalities, we solve each inequality separately and then find their intersection.\n\n- First, we solve $1 \\lt 3x-2 \\leq 7 \\,\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & <3x-2\\le 7 \\\\ 1+2 & <3x-2+2\\le 7+2 \\\\ 3 & <3x\\le 9 \\\\ \\frac{3}{3} & <\\frac{3x}{3}\\le \\frac{9}{3} \\\\ 1 & <x\\le 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/34/341633f5e132e1ab07af8969161c20443d65aec7e89ce0bc600868504dd19f9b.png)\n\n- Then, we solve  $2-3x \\leq -4 \\,\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2-3x & \\le -4 \\\\ 2-3x-2 & \\le -4-2 \\\\ -3x & \\le -6 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot (-3x) & \\ge (-1)\\cdot (-6) \\\\ 3x & \\ge 6 \\\\ \\frac{3x}{3} & \\ge \\frac{6}{3} \\\\ x & \\ge 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/06/06dafae801f6ed3900474c72437eb5a40376ed06bebf3c6eb568e6237c2d930d.png)\n\nTo find the values of $x$ that satisfy both inequalities, we find where the two solutions overlap:\n\n![](images/9b/9b3bd118d0940d6336a32c25b8556dccb3c4085f75da7d3d8628725cf9105071.png)\n\n   \n\nThus, the final solution is $x \\in [2,3].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510467 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064239 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c9460289-3e48-558e-b149-3e12a25e50a6" :knowledge-point/title "Flipping the Sign of an Inequality in a System"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "182b0266-a773-5415-8347-595d6e1d47b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z\\in (-2,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509733} {:answer/id #uuid "583f1205-51d8-5889-ae9f-97360c8da465" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z\\in (-\\infty ,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509871} {:answer/id #uuid "77d904be-ba18-55a6-9fa8-867bba7af7be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There is no solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509941} {:answer/id #uuid "cf0530c3-335a-560c-9890-ec8fda500e5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z\\in (-2,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510127} {:answer/id #uuid "f7766785-2d36-5b9e-b060-84124f5c69bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z\\in (-1,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510215}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "77d904be-ba18-55a6-9fa8-867bba7af7be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There is no solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509941} :answer-field/id #uuid "90ea46a7-9a19-5126-a84e-30034c4d5c82" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510311}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e87205b7-fd26-557d-b1a6-8478d490d3c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-156118" :question/problem "Find the set of values of $z$ that satisfy $1-z>3$ and $2z+1>5.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve the system, we solve each inequality separately and then find their intersection.\n\n- First, we solve $1-z>3:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-z & >3 \\\\ 1-z-1 & >3-1 \\\\ -z & >2 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot (-z) & <(-1)\\cdot 2 \\\\ z & <-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/72/72d4febdc48282faebade8f8a4b827a72b82433b054c6409752f892cb718ec85.png)\n\n- Then, we solve $2z+1>5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2z+1 & >5 \\\\ 2z+1-1 & >5-1 \\\\ 2z & >4 \\\\ \\frac{2z}{2} & >\\frac{4}{2} \\\\ z & >2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/84/84893a305567a0aaaafb6fd2393c62f05086780ce8c8a55b91ba68676ba309ce.png)\n\nTo find the values of $z$ that satisfy both inequalities, we find where the two solutions overlap:\n\n![](images/04/04b20be3eaf236e70aa5bdf8cf6e25b6838b3bb823fe16f926112fb1f5e02d6f.png)\n\nIt turns out that the solutions do not overlap at all. Therefore, there are no values of $z$ that satisfy both inequalities simultaneously. So, there is no solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510423 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064238 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "79f6f04e-ecce-5318-b72b-46478661ced0" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Systems of Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "168b9cb9-0b5a-5321-bc25-0ee1691fa73d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509729}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "168b9cb9-0b5a-5321-bc25-0ee1691fa73d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509729} :answer-field/id #uuid "cba0ab0d-68b9-5046-ba94-e69610135996" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510342} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e2be036-b7d4-513b-97ca-fbb936d6cff0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509961}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e2be036-b7d4-513b-97ca-fbb936d6cff0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509961} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4d2988b-6e70-5912-83af-e0291bc3bbdd" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510345}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8d7733a1-40a4-58cd-b679-edcbbad7631c" :question/math-academy-id "q-218745" :question/problem "What is the solution to the following system of inequalities?\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3t-2<-8 \\\\ t+1<-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution is\n$t$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "To solve the system, we need to find the values of $t$ that satisfy both $3t-2<-8$ and $t+1<-2$ simultaneously.\n\n- First, we solve $3t-2<-8\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3t-2 & <-8 \\\\ 3t-2+2 & <-8+2 \\\\ 3t & <-6 \\\\ \\frac{3t}{3} & <\\frac{-6}{3} \\\\ t & <-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/b9/b97b78ec613e826f7f8beb7336d3c2f285fc58d9bbf0c0f9d59921f41de2b3b6.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n- Then, we solve $t+1<-2\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t+1 & <-2 \\\\ t+1-1 & <-2-1 \\\\ t & <-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/cf/cfb26921afb706908f771e1934cf27c0ca6e248e9e3aca54f499af685393fa86.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $t$ that satisfy both inequalities, we find where the two solutions overlap:\n\n![](images/6d/6d488376420476cf34798aeb3fced46770a177288b550f2e887348c582741321.png)\n\n \n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nThus, the final solution is $t<-3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064605 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064240 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3286dfe-5140-5ba7-8e34-c98e63dc15c0" :knowledge-point/title "Systems Containing Compound Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b3b7fb3-6a14-5e6a-b22d-91c141148260" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509877}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5b3b7fb3-6a14-5e6a-b22d-91c141148260" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509877} :answer-field/id #uuid "f220bdb6-94ea-5c8c-8b3e-c792109f5378" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061710} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4bc2e4ef-81ec-5874-8cf2-75ca5d7c1420" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509844}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4bc2e4ef-81ec-5874-8cf2-75ca5d7c1420" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509844} :answer-field/id #uuid "111a1feb-4973-5295-afcc-add4bd2c219c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061711} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e880375-4c34-5d43-a662-388a73c5b705" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509962}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e880375-4c34-5d43-a662-388a73c5b705" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509962} :answer-field/id #uuid "53ba2e9b-e8b7-54b0-aab1-e28c9a2494cc" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061712}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5b65ad66-5f52-5406-9e2e-007075702256" :question/math-academy-id "q-220299" :question/problem "Find the set of values of $x$ that satisfy $-1\\le 2-x\\le 3$ and $2x+1\\ge 5.$\n\n{{field-1}}\n$\\le x$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "To solve compound \"and\" inequalities, we solve each inequality separately and then find their intersection.\n\n- First, we solve $-1\\le 2-x\\le 3\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le 2-x\\le 3 \\\\ -1-2 & \\le 2-x-2\\le 3-2 \\\\ -3 & \\le -x\\le 1 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot (-3) & \\ge (-1)\\cdot (-x)\\ge (-1)\\cdot 1 \\\\ 3 & \\ge x\\ge -1 \\\\ -1 & \\le x\\le 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/8f/8fe1b22970eac80550ae9cc8d2da4b34df6a853c717a7dd402b164dfd99356ce.png)\n\n- Then, we solve $2x+1\\ge 5\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+1 & \\ge 5 \\\\ 2x+1-1 & \\ge 5-1 \\\\ 2x & \\ge 4 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{2} & \\ge \\frac{4}{2} \\\\ x & \\ge 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/eb/ebcff9656b5f2a1fd80624639cb91baa0a28b696aa261b555cf449f1c62894d1.png)\n\nTo find the values of $x$ that satisfy both inequalities, we find where the two solutions overlap:\n\n![](images/77/7731bef503cf45a465945f81e0e2512f65c3e109a38d6d06afe74e17269f8c36.png)\n\nThus, the final solution is $2\\le x\\le 3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510458 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064237 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "53bf0d67-be51-5194-884b-e275d58a2ba1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection of Two Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d3a352e-0026-5fd0-b57a-2ee4ded5fa12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8b/8bc178b6dcfbc7dd36af32813847de4ecc85894c95eb7a6c53218a5ddf926e05.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509782} {:answer/id #uuid "49110c8e-ecd1-5c0f-9b5f-3032782e305f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/62/6281ea0ab80bf4a785d92026a5ccd0929659851e177e8cc7d6f41a7994a29791.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509837} {:answer/id #uuid "4d4d506c-989c-5ce8-a47e-9fd16c899779" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509846} {:answer/id #uuid "5be1f5c8-81c4-539d-9fe0-466cb70fe3a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/85/857598f76c6c06c3d4dd345700bd46e63c855ea3af2d48b5b52b3473fccabdce.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509880} {:answer/id #uuid "60fb93e9-ddcc-5501-af28-4f45463dfb7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0d/0dd8dc2d8580100a728ef0406bf953670aee7787bb2d0e2c2a21ca454725d294.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509889}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60fb93e9-ddcc-5501-af28-4f45463dfb7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0d/0dd8dc2d8580100a728ef0406bf953670aee7787bb2d0e2c2a21ca454725d294.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509889} :answer-field/id #uuid "841ef974-3800-52e9-afb8-592ab264e005" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510307}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d7abcd6f-c9ce-5a9a-8667-2f8c0c4481fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-25599" :question/problem "Which number line shows the values of $x$ that satisfy $2x-7<5$ and $3x+3\\ge -3?$" :question/worked-solution "To solve compound \"and\" inequalities, we solve each inequality separately and then find their intersection. \n\n- First, we solve $2x-7<5\\,:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-7 & <5 \\\\ 2x-7+7 & <5+7 \\\\ 2x & <12 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{2} & <\\frac{12}{2} \\\\ x & <6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/c3/c3f9a8f8d42c4e029fd7d5ce26ef05d9834f6bf443aa61c1e3a89d228e79efc5.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n- Then, we solve $3x+3\\ge -3\\,:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+3 & \\ge -3 \\\\ 3x+3-3 & \\ge -3-3 \\\\ 3x & \\ge -6 \\\\ \\frac{3x}{3} & \\ge \\frac{-6}{3} \\\\ x & \\ge -2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/62/6281ea0ab80bf4a785d92026a5ccd0929659851e177e8cc7d6f41a7994a29791.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $x$ that satisfy both inequalities, we find where the two solutions overlap:\n\n![](images/1d/1da1439e3fff4e39a6b891d8b295eada7e67b49763bca0b080a076c833242d7e.png)\n\nThus, the final solution is $-2\\le x<6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510367 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064237 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "53bf0d67-be51-5194-884b-e275d58a2ba1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection of Two Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5607bd9f-094b-52df-9b8f-b5360356f13c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1<x<3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509866} {:answer/id #uuid "5c190c3b-2061-54ec-a536-390502430e73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3<x<1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509881} {:answer/id #uuid "709243d9-405b-5d1e-9eca-058aca83cabe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x<0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509919} {:answer/id #uuid "a563c648-2b23-5eee-ab23-59a4ebc2ed85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There is no solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510034} {:answer/id #uuid "c9c14257-676a-5895-b3f4-45d10dc5348c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1<x<1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510111}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c9c14257-676a-5895-b3f4-45d10dc5348c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1<x<1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510111} :answer-field/id #uuid "8807da01-297f-5334-a2ec-d198f503b63f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510309}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0629bbb0-2921-5d85-ab43-d50c29c16b81" :question/math-academy-id "q-51741" :question/problem "Find the values of $x$ that satisfy $7x>-7$ and $3x<3.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve compound \"and\" inequalities, we solve each inequality separately and then find their intersection. \n\n- First, we solve $7x>-7\\,:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7x & >-7 \\\\ \\frac{7x}{7} & >\\frac{-7}{7} \\\\ x & >-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/9b/9b902e22e6808cf01993494e199b9fcbd184d084e385ef94cb9a1953c00abb7c.png)\n\n- Then, we solve $3x<3\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x & <3 \\\\ \\frac{3x}{3} & >\\frac{3}{3} \\\\ x & <1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/ca/ca26af3420f15a115c44ddb234afe4226e850799b5f91625faaee4c4fad37a4a.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $x$ that satisfy both inequalities, we find where the two solutions overlap:\n\n![](images/12/12b3a4dedd88b66e7c06812b83c3195e889bdf22d40e45432e8569aaf5764047.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nThus, the final solution is $-1<x<1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510436 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064238 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "79f6f04e-ecce-5318-b72b-46478661ced0" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Systems of Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01e27701-894d-5377-af37-c37f1f254842" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2<x\\le 7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509698} {:answer/id #uuid "8d320ee1-75ce-5deb-9ea2-410b499994b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7\\le x<-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509994} {:answer/id #uuid "b4f67fdb-16f0-5e5b-8a9c-e41c37a3fd25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2<x\\le 7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510077} {:answer/id #uuid "e5497ec0-c287-5185-8021-dcc987cc188e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\le x<7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510173} {:answer/id #uuid "ec7071aa-4a9c-591d-87df-d455d836a762" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7<x\\le 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510199}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "01e27701-894d-5377-af37-c37f1f254842" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2<x\\le 7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509698} :answer-field/id #uuid "104238e8-9c93-53a1-911b-7297525db4c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510244}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a6038f4d-7120-5131-9e5c-91d2792ec538" :question/math-academy-id "q-76000" :question/problem "What is the solution to the following system of inequalities?\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}4x-2>6 \\\\ 2x-9\\le 5\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve the system, we need to find the values of $x$ that satisfy both $4x-2>6$ and $2x-9\\le 5$ simultaneously.\n\n- First, we solve $4x-2>6\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-2 & >6 \\\\ 4x-2+2 & >6+2 \\\\ 4x & >8 \\\\ \\frac{4x}{4} & >\\frac{8}{4} \\\\ x & >2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/59/59523e51144ef776295ec43032def1bc0192351deb6294fbb2d56acd87bb2cac.png)\n\n- Then, we solve $2x-9\\le 5\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-9 & \\le 5 \\\\ 2x-9+9 & \\le 5 \\\\ 2x & \\le 14 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{2} & \\le \\frac{14}{2} \\\\ x & \\le 7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/b0/b0107bec7ccb2c56036de405a29870e8cfcc166cc6405f425fc3296ec8f1be2b.png)\n\nTo find the values of $x$ that satisfy both inequalities, we find where the two solutions overlap:\n\n![](images/f9/f9ace3f6dd9d93b960c61bb31ca3858aefbb0e8d43f2392a643c078ae6111a0d.png)\n\nThus, the final solution is $2<x\\le 7.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510442 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064239 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c9460289-3e48-558e-b149-3e12a25e50a6" :knowledge-point/title "Flipping the Sign of an Inequality in a System"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "359641cf-22bc-507d-af66-eb57e6b8acb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-2,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509804} {:answer/id #uuid "748d9863-150c-5850-9738-ed30a65b54cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-2,2]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509934} {:answer/id #uuid "89fb18e0-e809-5f6e-87f3-671a7008175e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There is no solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509990} {:answer/id #uuid "a2d271bf-fcb0-5786-9bf4-9a7e39ea439d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,2]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510026} {:answer/id #uuid "fa5b9543-e03b-5065-9082-1691603a581e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-2,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510225}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "89fb18e0-e809-5f6e-87f3-671a7008175e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There is no solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509990} :answer-field/id #uuid "2be5b73b-52ea-5b0e-85cd-1bd1f22b7b52" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510256}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ae0becce-68fd-5837-9300-0c55dedc4632" :question/math-academy-id "q-76004" :question/problem "Find the set of values of $x$ that satisfy $4x+9\\ge 1$ and $1-3x>7.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve the system, we solve each inequality separately and then find their intersection.\n\n- First, we solve $4x+9\\ge 1\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+9 & \\ge 1 \\\\ 4x+9-9 & \\ge 1-9 \\\\ 4x & \\ge -8 \\\\ \\frac{4x}{4} & \\ge \\frac{-8}{4} \\\\ x & \\ge -2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/16/1673c69df6497fd90ddab9c51c208ca5110f0e3c5a03a101e3b46723e04081fe.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n- Then, we solve $1-3x>7\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-3x & >7 \\\\ 1-3x-1 & >7-1 \\\\ -3x & >6 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot (-3x) & <(-1)\\cdot 6 \\\\ 3x & <-6 \\\\ \\frac{3x}{3} & <\\frac{-6}{3} \\\\ x & <-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/b9/b97b78ec613e826f7f8beb7336d3c2f285fc58d9bbf0c0f9d59921f41de2b3b6.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $x$ that satisfy both inequalities, we find where the two solutions overlap:\n\n![](images/54/544d23551ed218c0d7e373ba0d04dbe1ad51d587c452b875c1a45df2e896cd87.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nIt turns out that the solutions do not overlap at all. Therefore, there are no values of $x$ that satisfy both inequalities simultaneously. So, there is no solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510429 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064240 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3286dfe-5140-5ba7-8e34-c98e63dc15c0" :knowledge-point/title "Systems Containing Compound Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2132bf72-52a3-5430-9d30-39b5d22fafc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [1,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509753} {:answer/id #uuid "23a3f9fe-829f-5f5d-8b8d-0e61573b6c63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (2,3]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509764} {:answer/id #uuid "82c7c6aa-4d8a-5782-a1fb-132c9e204e1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-1,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509975} {:answer/id #uuid "ce9ff232-8ba8-5c0c-baca-726f324f8f30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There is no solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510124} {:answer/id #uuid "d5f76f38-964b-5b3e-933f-7a5896b7eabe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-2)\\cup (-2,3]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510143}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce9ff232-8ba8-5c0c-baca-726f324f8f30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There is no solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510124} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa640ad7-cabb-5499-80c5-a48dcfe57f99" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510359}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a0a0618e-ff8d-55ba-915b-f7de9b4bbbc9" :question/math-academy-id "q-76010" :question/problem "Find the set of values of $x$ that satisfy $-1<2x-3\\le 1$ and $3x>9.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve compound \"and\" inequalities, we solve each inequality separately and then find their intersection.\n\n- First, we solve $-1<2x-3\\le 1\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & <2x-3\\le 1 \\\\ -1+3 & <2x-3+3\\le 1+3 \\\\ 2 & <2x\\le 4 \\\\ \\frac{2}{2} & <\\frac{2x}{2}\\le \\frac{4}{2} \\\\ 1 & <x\\le 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/7f/7f940af7e7480f83d89f47b53ec1f9b9d9d23e93d8419464055ada7b77c22be1.png)\n\n- Then, we solve  $3x>9\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x & >9 \\\\ \\frac{3x}{3} & >\\frac{9}{3} \\\\ x & >3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/08/0883c587c9c164cc35fdf17b07f0d0bd3767c715c8c537e3c1013239194f22bc.png)\n\nTo find the values of $x$ that satisfy both inequalities, we find where the two solutions overlap:\n\n![](images/5d/5d31a9ebff15e2eb52faf5e3768576cf2de60205882fc130efb57f77ffad0b96.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nIt turns out that the solutions do not overlap at all. Therefore, there are no values of $x$ that satisfy both inequalities simultaneously. So, there is no solution."}]}
